{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/connector at 9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690 on request/github-connector-render. Replaces artifact 254986d011d3115336ae85d5ca05182180e891c5, which named this same head and was stale from birth.\n\nRefiled for its basis, not its content. The predecessor rested on the assert that corrected my false claim, and that assert rests on a report of the head I had just superseded — so the artifact was stale the moment it was written, and gs merge refuses a stale artifact. An approval against it could not have been acted on, which would have wasted a review rather than merely looked untidy. This one rests on the governing request alone, which is live and not stale. The assert is still the honest record of the correction; it is simply not a load-bearing anchor for the thing it describes.\n\nWhat the head does, unchanged from the withdrawn artifact. The charter gate no longer refuses a stale charter, which the predecessor commit had left refusing one layer above the clause admission it repaired. Every charter an operator states correctly is stale from the moment it is written, because a replacement must cite what it replaces and what it replaces is then retired, so refusing there rejected the charter before admission was ever reached and no operator could state one that worked. Staleness is now reported to whoever runs the connector. Retirement and absent ratification still refuse, because those withdraw authority rather than move underneath it.\n\nThe proposal coherence check deliberately still refuses a stale request or artifact. A pull request naming a stale artifact tells a public reader it is current when its basis has moved, and unlike a charter nothing makes an artifact stale by construction. Staleness therefore blocks in exactly one place, and where that line belongs is the question I have asked codex to settle.\n\nThe expectation that a stale charter is refused is replaced rather than deleted, and mutation-checked by restoring the refusal.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","commit":"9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690","head":"9f30db4245ea2831297de51840343e9e3699b690","path":"internal/connector"}}